```mermaid
%% State Machine Diagram: Order Lifecycle
%% Based on Chapter 4 — Domain Analysis

stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Address: create cart / start checkout

    Address --> Delivery: set shipping address
    Address --> [*]: cancel

    Delivery --> Payment: select shipping method
    Delivery --> [*]: cancel

    Payment --> Confirm: select payment method
    Payment --> [*]: cancel

    Confirm --> Complete: confirm order
    Confirm --> [*]: cancel

    Complete --> [*]: order finalized

    note right of Address
        CheckoutState enum values:
        Address, Delivery, Payment, Confirm, Complete
    end note

    note right of Complete
        Order.Status becomes Draft or Pending
        Finalized orders are immutable
        except for Cancel transition
    end note
```

## Diagram Description

The Order checkout state machine enforces **monotonic progression** — states only move forward. This invariant is encoded in domain methods (`Order.Method.Checkout.cs`) and validated in the `CreateOrderFromCart` handler.

**Business rule**: "CheckoutState progresses forward; Finalized orders are immutable except Cancel" (`Order.cs:12`).

**Evidence**: `Module/Ordering/Domain/Orders/Order.cs:20`, `Order.Constant.cs:50-56`, `Order.Method.Checkout.cs`
